## 6. No Requirement to Pay

Except where a specific feature or service is explicitly designated as paid, users are not required to pay for the basic use of the application.

The copyright holders may provide certain functionality without charge and may subsequently introduce optional paid functionality.

Nothing in this License guarantees that every feature of every future version will remain free.

## 7. Privacy and Data Minimization

OpenOBC is designed according to the principle of data minimization.

The application shall not intentionally collect personal or technical data unless such data is reasonably necessary for:

- the correct operation of the application;
- communication with compatible OpenOBC hardware;
- configuration or operation of OpenOBC firmware;
- diagnostics explicitly requested by the user;
- security and abuse prevention;
- compatibility and reliability of the application; or
- a feature explicitly enabled or requested by the user.

The application shall not intentionally collect data solely because it is technically possible to collect it.

## 8. No Sale of User Data

Data obtained through the OpenOBC mobile application shall not be sold to third parties for any purpose.

The copyright holders shall not sell, rent, license, broker, or otherwise commercially trade user data.

This prohibition applies regardless of whether the data is collected directly by the application or through an OpenOBC-operated service.

Nothing in this section prohibits the use of third-party infrastructure providers strictly as necessary to operate the application or provide a requested service, provided that such providers do not receive rights to sell or commercially trade the user's data.

## 9. Data Required for Operation

Where data is necessary for the correct operation of the application or OpenOBC firmware, the application may process such data to the extent reasonably necessary for that purpose.

Examples may include:

- Bluetooth identifiers required to establish a connection;
- OpenOBC device identifiers;
- firmware version information;
- vehicle telemetry required to display requested information;
- diagnostic information required to perform a requested operation;
- application configuration;
- crash information necessary to diagnose application failures; and
- security information required to authenticate or protect communication.

The application should avoid retaining such information longer than reasonably necessary for the stated purpose.

## 10. User-Controlled Data

Where technically feasible, information generated by the application for the user's use, including vehicle telemetry, diagnostic information, configuration data, logs, and trip information, should remain under the user's control and may be stored locally on the user's device.

The application shall not transmit such information to OpenOBC-operated infrastructure unless transmission is necessary for a feature requested or enabled by the user, required for operation, or separately disclosed to the user.

## 11. Privacy Policy

The detailed handling of personal data and other information shall be described in the OpenOBC Privacy Policy.

Where applicable, the Privacy Policy shall identify:

- categories of data collected;
- purposes of collection;
- data retention periods;
- third parties receiving data;
- storage locations;
- security measures;
- user rights;
- optional telemetry or analytics;
- advertising technologies; and
- mechanisms for deleting or controlling user data.

If there is a conflict between this License and mandatory privacy or data-protection law, the applicable law shall prevail.

## 12. Advertising

The Official Version may contain advertising in future releases.

Advertising may be provided directly by OpenOBC or through third-party advertising services.

The presence of advertising does not grant advertisers ownership of OpenOBC or user data.

Advertising providers shall only receive information to the extent necessary to provide the advertising functionality and as disclosed by the applicable Privacy Policy.

The copyright holders may provide an option to disable advertising through an optional payment, subscription, donation, or other mechanism.

## 13. Donations and Optional Payments

The copyright holders may accept voluntary donations.

Donations do not constitute a purchase of the Software or transfer ownership of any intellectual property.

The copyright holders may also offer optional paid features, services, integrations, or other functionality.

A payment for an optional feature grants only the rights explicitly associated with that feature and does not grant rights to the underlying source code or intellectual property.

